  "mach:trainingDataSummary": "33 million normal human cells from CellXGene spanning brain, blood, heart, lung, kidney, and pan-cancer tissue types. Pre-trained checkpoints available per tissue type and as a whole-human model.",
  "mach:intendedUse": "Single-cell genomics research: cell type annotation, multi-omics integration, gene regulatory network analysis. Research use. Not a cleared medical device.",
